 "text": "Hi, how have you been? Once upon time, far away in the woods, there stood an old cabin, haunted by ghostly lights and sounds at night. One dark evening, a group of brave explorers reached the cabin, their goal to hunt for treasure in the ruins. He was. He'd been haunting the cabin for a hundred years, his ghost lamp still burning as he watched over his stolen treasure. Probably. The explorers spent the night in the cabin, each one seeing or hearing things they couldn't explain. Sure. Why don't ghosts ever go on vacation? Because they believe in haunting every corner. Off they go, out of the haunted house and onto a sun kissed beach.",
